\label{lem:finite-complete}
The periodic complex $(U_j,\Delta_j)$ is exact and remains exact
after tensoring with every injective $\Lambda_j^{\mathrm{op}}$-module.

\label{cor:duality-failures}
\label{cor:Hom-injective}
\label{cor:no-preenvelope}
Let $R$ be the ring in \eqref{eq:main-ring}. Then neither $\mathcal{GF}(R)$ nor
$\mathcal{GI}(R^{\mathrm{op}})$ nor the class of Ding injective $R^{\mathrm{op}}$-modules is
definable.

There are a pure-injective Ding injective module $E$ and an injective module
$I$ such that $\operatorname{Gfd}_R\operatorname{Hom}_{R^{\mathrm{op}}}(E,I)=\infty$.

The module $M$ has neither a Gorenstein flat preenvelope nor a
projectively coresolved Gorenstein flat preenvelope.

\label{prop:canonical-bidual}
Let $R$ be a right coherent ring. Then the following conditions are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The class $\mathcal{GF}(R)$ is closed under direct products.
\item The module $C_U^\rho$ is Gorenstein flat.
\item The module $C_U^{++}$ is Gorenstein flat.
\item $\operatorname{Gfd}_RC_U^{++}<\infty$.
\item The module $E_U^{++}$ is Gorenstein injective.
\item $\operatorname{Gid}_{R^{\mathrm{op}}}E_U^{++}<\infty$.
\end{enumerate}
